cat > README.md <<'E'
# cli-todo-app

Node.js todo CLI (no dependencies, Node 18+). Data lives in `todos.json` in the current directory.

```
node index.js add "Buy groceries"
node index.js list
node index.js complete 1
node index.js delete 1
npm test
```

`list` prints `<id> [x|space] <text>`. Errors go to stderr with exit code 1.

## Design decisions

- `index.js` is the entry point, `src/cli.js` dispatches commands, `src/todos.js` holds pure logic, `src/storage.js` does file I/O.
- New ids are max id + 1, so deleting the newest todo lets its id be reused, but ids of remaining todos never change.
- Each todo: `id`, `text`, `completed`, `createdAt` (ISO 8601).
- Writes go to a temp file then rename, so a crash cannot leave a truncated `todos.json`.
- A corrupt `todos.json` is reported and never overwritten.
- Completing an already-completed todo succeeds silently.
- Isolation: the store is per-directory. Set `TODOS_FILE` to use a different file.
- Only one id algorithm (max+1) is implemented; a counter or UUID would add state or break the integer-id requirement.
- Concurrent writers are not locked; last write wins.
E
